      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=4.5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
      "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=4.5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{4.5}{2}=2.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=4.5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|2.25|=2.25$ centered at the point $(0,2.25),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253930/assets/7fe3619c1118b553a33ccceff2afd6f1429fe763afce1ec725bd18be7f3c196c.png)",
